=============================================================================

.vercelignore — Vercel builds ONLY the Expo web frontend from this repository.

=============================================================================

WHY THIS FILE EXISTS

The backend (backend/) is a LONG-RUNNING Node HTTP server. It needs:

* node:sqlite + the --experimental-sqlite flag

* a writable, private (0700) directory for the SQLite file

* a background worker process (queue)

None of that is possible on Vercel Serverless Functions, so Vercel must never

try to bundle backend/*.mjs. When it does, the bundler copies only the entry

file and then fails to resolve the sibling relative imports, producing:

[RESOLVE_ERROR] Could not resolve './auth/security.mjs'

[RESOLVE_ERROR] Could not resolve './auth/lifecycle.mjs'

[RESOLVE_ERROR] Could not resolve './queue/queue.mjs'

[RESOLVE_ERROR] Could not resolve './runners/code-runner.mjs'

Excluding the backend here removes it from the Vercel build entirely.

=============================================================================

Backend + all non-frontend code

backend/
legacy/
execution-core/
phase2-core/
scripts/
test/
docs/
infra/
data/


Tooling / CI / caches

node_modules/
.expo/
.expo-shared/
.github/
coverage/
*.tsbuildinfo


Docs & archives (never shipped to the CDN)

*.md
*.zip
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-*


Local secrets (defence in depth — these are also git-ignored)

.env
.env.*
!.env.example
